#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Step 14, run 3b of effect-slot-refactor.md: rewrites the agent-docs rows (and the two skills' guidance) that describe
step 12a part 2's "whenever [an object] enters" abilities with trigger-only wrappers, the way
scripts/step14-enters-options.py rewrote the cards: a condition on the entering object becomes the trigger's filter
(the permanent form of the old card predicate; the two-argument TriggeringPermanentConditionalEffect on
enters(null, ANY) also meant "you control", so those become YOU_CONTROL), "this creature or another [X] you control"
the relation THIS_OR_ANOTHER_YOU_CONTROL (or ANOTHER_YOU_CONTROL beside an enters(THIS) trigger), a limit a
TriggerLimit and an intervening "if" a TriggerOptions (or onlyDuringYourTurn() for "during your turn"). The deleted
EnteringCreature* / EnteringLand* wrapper rows are replaced by rows for the filter form, and
PermanentEnteredOrCastFromZonePredicate / PermanentWasCastPredicate get rows in PREDICATES_REFERENCE.md. Rows of cards
that keep their wrapper (Sigil Captain, Akim the Soaring Wind, Phyrexian Dragon Engine, Archfiend's Vessel, Oasis of
Renewal, Field of the Dead, Archaeomancer's Map, Confounding Conundrum, Invader Parasite, Tunnel Ignus), of cards whose
wrapper the card conversion did not reach (Nature's Wrath, Oran-Rief Hydra, Emeria Shepherd) and of other trigger
families are left alone. Each replacement must match exactly once; one whose new text is already present is
skipped, so the script can be run again.

Usage: python3 scripts/step14-enters-docs.py
"""
